WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.209 --> 00:00:01.042
- I did it.

00:00:01.042 --> 00:00:03.212
And I'm comfortable and I travel.

00:00:03.212 --> 00:00:06.089
It's a good life. It's such a good life.

00:00:06.089 --> 00:00:09.229
(gentle music)

00:00:09.229 --> 00:00:10.121
I'm 70.

00:00:10.121 --> 00:00:11.189
- I am 70.

00:00:11.189 --> 00:00:12.699
- 71 years old.

00:00:12.699 --> 00:00:13.972
- Best years of my life.

00:00:13.972 --> 00:00:15.926
- 70 is not bad. (chuckles)

00:00:15.926 --> 00:00:18.832
- I feel I'm right in
between feeling really old

00:00:18.832 --> 00:00:20.068
and still feeling young enough

00:00:20.068 --> 00:00:22.733
to be able to do the
things that I wanna do.

00:00:22.733 --> 00:00:25.309
(gentle music)

00:00:25.309 --> 00:00:27.524
- I wanted a position that
there weren't many people

00:00:27.524 --> 00:00:29.549
in that position that looked like me.

00:00:29.549 --> 00:00:31.660
When I bid for the position, she was like,

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:33.410
I don't know if you can do this.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:35.505
I looked around the department

00:00:35.505 --> 00:00:36.500
and I saw the people doing

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.488
and I said, well aren't those
humans sitting at the desk?

00:00:39.488 --> 00:00:43.025
I'm human so I can do it too.

00:00:43.025 --> 00:00:45.963
The rest is history as I
say, that was 31 years ago.

00:00:45.963 --> 00:00:48.029
- I married the same person three times

00:00:48.029 --> 00:00:49.464
and so I put my children through

00:00:49.464 --> 00:00:52.805
some very unpleasant experiences.

00:00:52.805 --> 00:00:54.233
- At the age of 61,

00:00:54.233 --> 00:00:57.527
I was diagnosed with a
rare and aggressive cancer.

00:00:57.527 --> 00:01:01.321
I definitely felt my
mortality's on this balancing,

00:01:01.321 --> 00:01:03.402
doing the things that
I believe in and enjoy

00:01:03.402 --> 00:01:06.753
with not knowing how much longer
I'm gonna be able to do it.

00:01:06.753 --> 00:01:09.191
- With the divorce and
going back and forth

00:01:09.191 --> 00:01:13.707
for three times, okay I
wasn't ready to give up on it.

00:01:13.707 --> 00:01:17.504
But there came a time where
I needed to give up on it.

00:01:17.504 --> 00:01:19.778
You have to forgive yourself.

00:01:19.778 --> 00:01:22.631
(gentle music)

00:01:22.631 --> 00:01:26.809
- The city was trying to condemn
this low income residence.

00:01:26.809 --> 00:01:28.865
We're able to re-habit.

00:01:28.865 --> 00:01:31.510
What was nice for me was
seeing this first generation

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:33.465
Japanese immigrant woman,

00:01:33.465 --> 00:01:36.146
when she moved back into
her apartment, was in tears.

00:01:36.146 --> 00:01:38.122
- I feel like I was a
much better grandmother

00:01:38.122 --> 00:01:39.769
than I was mother.

00:01:39.769 --> 00:01:42.242
I know when my daughter
moved, I spent that hour

00:01:42.242 --> 00:01:44.224
crying because I wasn't going to have

00:01:44.224 --> 00:01:46.908
my granddaughter there and my grandson.

00:01:46.908 --> 00:01:48.905
And that's when I
reduced my hours at work.

00:01:48.905 --> 00:01:52.499
I said I'm not gonna be a
grandma that they don't know.

00:01:52.499 --> 00:01:53.486
- Being a coordinator,
I tell them, you know,

00:01:53.486 --> 00:01:56.389
let me know if it's not a
good fit and I'll change you.

00:01:56.389 --> 00:01:58.178
So one little boy, the
tutor wanted to be changed

00:01:58.178 --> 00:02:00.545
'cause she said he asks
too many questions.

00:02:00.545 --> 00:02:01.721
So I took him.

00:02:01.721 --> 00:02:02.691
And when I took him, it was that I found

00:02:02.691 --> 00:02:04.088
that he was just very intelligent.

00:02:04.088 --> 00:02:05.457
He was very inquisitive.

00:02:05.457 --> 00:02:07.710
But really got to me though was that

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:09.932
one week when we came back,
he came in the door and said,

00:02:09.932 --> 00:02:12.067
I'm a genius, I'm a genius.

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:14.603
And I was like tears, like now.

00:02:14.603 --> 00:02:16.860
He said I got 100% on my spelling test.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:19.473
And I thought that was just phew,

00:02:19.473 --> 00:02:22.226
I did that. I helped him do that.

00:02:22.226 --> 00:02:24.406
(gentle music)

00:02:24.406 --> 00:02:28.008
The misconception that so
many young people have is that

00:02:28.008 --> 00:02:31.021
when you grow old, everything
... you lose stuff.

00:02:31.021 --> 00:02:32.290
You don't.

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:35.197
Your mind and your desires and your drives

00:02:35.197 --> 00:02:37.121
stay the same, they're there.

00:02:37.121 --> 00:02:40.496
It's just that your body
can't fulfill (chuckles)

00:02:40.496 --> 00:02:41.440
those wishes.

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:45.147
But I went zip lining at 55 years old.

00:02:45.147 --> 00:02:47.389
And I mean it was an adventure.

00:02:47.389 --> 00:02:49.634
I was mature age but just go for it.

00:02:49.634 --> 00:02:52.052
- You know in the night before my surgery,

00:02:52.052 --> 00:02:55.102
where they did not know
what they were gonna find.

00:02:55.102 --> 00:02:56.534
They knew it was a large tumor.

00:02:56.534 --> 00:02:58.668
Some of the things I said,
you know I've got a good life.

00:02:58.668 --> 00:03:00.442
It's a life of purpose.

00:03:00.442 --> 00:03:02.842
It's a life of doing
the things I believe in.

00:03:02.842 --> 00:03:05.684
- I don't have a bucket list anymore.

00:03:05.684 --> 00:03:08.158
I may have something tomorrow
that I never thought,

00:03:08.158 --> 00:03:10.000
oh maybe I wanna do that.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.427
I'm living my bucket list daily.

00:03:11.427 --> 00:03:13.545
I'm doing what I wanna do right now.

00:03:13.545 --> 00:03:15.009
- When one dies, you know,

00:03:15.009 --> 00:03:16.764
you don't look at the date of birth

00:03:16.764 --> 00:03:18.365
and the date when they died.

00:03:18.365 --> 00:03:20.374
But you look at the dash in between

00:03:20.374 --> 00:03:21.414
and that's what's important,

00:03:21.414 --> 00:03:23.945
is what did they do during that life?

00:03:23.945 --> 00:03:28.195
Don't let the passions
that fueled you (chuckles)

00:03:28.195 --> 00:03:30.350
when you were younger die out.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:32.426
- Go boldly into the future

00:03:32.426 --> 00:03:34.982
and boldly into your maturity

00:03:34.982 --> 00:03:36.588
because it's a wonderful thing.

00:03:36.588 --> 00:03:39.476
It's life cycle, it's wonderful.

00:03:39.476 --> 00:03:43.041
Embrace it. It's cool, I'm happy.

00:03:43.041 --> 00:03:45.624
(gentle music)

